<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Compagnie de Saint-Christophe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1626">1626</a>–<a href="/years/1635">1635</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Company of Saint Christopher</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Compagnie de Saint-Christophe was a French colonial company founded in 1626 under the patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a> to settle and exploit the island of Saint Christopher (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a>) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-belain-desnambuc">Pierre Belain d'Esnambuc</a> led its colonists, who shared the island with the English. Short of capital, it was reorganised in 1635 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compagnie-des-iles-de-lamerique">Compagnie des Îles de l'Amérique</a>, which extended French settlement to Martinique and Guadeloupe.</p></div>
